title The sixteenth rung stays home, and a fold is priced on what a body reaches
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first under Standfast, deep-read one council-rota row, refresh the live card, and send.
think Standfast opened the lap. The Caravan choir ran at HEAD before a line moved and sang GREEN at 108, and the era suite ran GREEN at ten rungs, both run rather than trusted. crux/REDS.md reads closed through %131 with no agent-closable red standing.
think The running thread came off the top three rows of session-logs/README.md. The newest recommend named apprise_the_raiser at fifteen identical bodies over sixteen declarations -- 658 by realized fall, zero widening -- and asked the lap to open by reading which rung differs and why before folding the fifteen.
think Ran tools/fixtures/ladder_reach_visibility_scan.sh apprise_the_raiser first. REACH_OK named folding=15 widens=0 stub=3 fall=658, and hashing the sixteen bodies gave two digests: fifteen at one, caravan/apprise.rye alone at another.
think Diffed the odd rung against the cohort. Seven lines differ and nothing else does -- apprise.rye writes report_out.apprised where the fifteen write apprise_of(report_out).apprised, because in that rung the apprise report IS the report and no accessor stands between them. That is a difference of meaning, so the rung keeps its own body rather than gaining an accessor it has no use for.
think The harness gained pub fn apprise_the_raiser(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, apprise: rung.Apprise, report_out: *rung.Report) (rung.RunError || rung.NoteError)!void, reaching thirteen helpers -- redress_written, apprise_of, unheard_findings, apprised_in, unsent_in, max_address_len, address_published, found_bytes, found_answers, apprise_refusal, apprise_note, apprise_holds, apprised_of -- through the type handed in. It sits beside its kin read_the_finding, book_the_debt, say_the_word, and meet_the_debt, which share its shape exactly.
think Each of the fifteen rungs keeps its own full doc comment and a three-line stub returning ladder_checks.apprise_the_raiser(@This(), io, apprise, report_out). The docs stayed home deliberately: each names what that rung's own apprising proves, and the carry meter reads code lines rather than comments, so moving them would have widened the round without moving the number.
think Three living claims moved with the code. The carry scan's default ceiling came down from 73,825 to 73,167, the carry witness's two pinned lines moved to the measured carry and body counts, and the reach-visibility witness advanced one lap -- its folded slot took apprise_the_raiser, its head slot redress_the_meeting, its sibling slot weigh_the_answer.
think The head slot's first claim was wrong on its first run. I wrote redress_the_meeting as sixteen declarations holding sixteen identical bodies; the scan reads declared=17 identical=16, so a seventeenth rung writes a different body there too. Corrected before the witness ran, and the next lap now opens on the same question this one did.
obs Prediction met measurement to the digit for the third lap running under the meter. Carry 73,819 -> 73,161, a fall of exactly 658; delegates 2,984 -> 2,999, exactly the fifteen stubs; bodies 18,166 -> 18,167; distinct 7,963 -> 7,964; ceiling down to 73,167.
obs The derivation is fourteen bodies times forty-seven lines. One body survives in the harness and each stub costs three, so a family folding n at k lines returns (n-1)(k-3) -- which is why a short ladder carrying a long body outranks a long ladder carrying a short one on this queue.
obs Run against the folded family afterward, the same scan reads widens=15 fall=0 -- a stub reaches ladder_checks, which stands private in each rung. So the queue reports a door already through rather than offering it a second time.
obs The split-on-one-qualifier shape has now appeared three laps running -- entrust.rye and confer.rye stayed home from the confirm lift, apprise.rye stays home from this one, and the scan already names a seventeenth rung differing under redress_the_meeting. A cohort is read at the head of the lap and its outliers are read for meaning, never assumed to be accident.
obs Council rota, row one -- Air and Saturn, law and boundary. TAME Core's smallest-scope rule and this fold are the same move: one body, reached through the rung handed in, rather than fifteen a reader must diff to trust. Single-strandedness named the trade exactly -- the harness and the rung compose side by side through one contract word, rung, and neither braids into the other. And Conway explained why the arc records every number rather than remembering it: an organization whose members forget nightly replaces a claim with a program that re-proves itself, which is what the widening meter is.
obs No red booked this lap. The head-slot correction was caught by running the scan rather than by trusting the sentence I had just written, which is the ordinary ratchet of this arc rather than a defect.
